	title = {Virtual {Assistant} {System} in {Banking} {Application} {With} {Fine}-{Tuned} {LLM} and {RAG} {Approach}},
	isbn = {2837-5203},
	doi = {10.1109/ICIMCIS68501.2025.11327124},
	abstract = {The rapid growth of digital financial services has changed the way people handle their banking services. Although these digital platforms offer more efficiency, they have also created a digital literacy gap for users in Generation X, Millennials, and Gen Z. To address this issue, this research presents the design of a Virtual Assistant for banking applications. Where built to be intuitive by mimicking the user-friendly experience of common chat platforms like WhatsApp. Uses Large Language Models (LLM) to deliver high-quality customer support, with two primary key improvements. First, an advanced RetrievalAugmented Generation (RAG) system. Ablation study tests show that implementation of hybrid search, recursive chunking, and data cleaning achieved the highest performance score of 0.572. Second, fine-tuned LLM function call using a custom database in Bahasa Indonesia. This significantly boosted its performance, outperforming other top models in three categories on the Gorilla Berkeley Function Call benchmark. The system’s architecture is based on a Multi-Agent Orchestrated Pipeline, making it both powerful and reliable. Ultimately, this work contributes to building smarter and more inclusive digital banking solutions for everyone.},
