	abstract = {The existing healthcare chatbots do not assist medical practice in real-life as they operate only through textual interaction and do not have multimodal understanding. This paper presents a multimodal AI-based medical chatbot that will interpret both speech and skin images and text messages within a unified conversational framework.The suggested system combines a speech-to-text transcription with the help of OpenAI Whisper, multimodal reasoning with the help of Meta LLaMA-3 Vision, and a Gradio-based interface allowing users to interact in real time through both textual and voice responses that are generated with the help of gTTS and ElevenLabs. According to experimental results, there is high accuracy of response, low latency, and multimodal congruence, which is able to provide reliable performance in early medical direction. The chatbot is medically safe and ethically used since it is designed as a decision-support system and not as a diagnostic tool. The most important contribution of this work is the development of a modular, scalable, and context-aware multimodal healthcare chatbot to increase the level of accessibility, the quality of interaction and usage in online healthcare support systems. © 2026 IEEE.},
