	doi = {10.1109/ICOT68409.2025.11425595},
	abstract = {Cross-border e-commerce requires scalable content creation and efficient multilingual customer service to support global buyers. Traditional workflows rely heavily on manual labor, which increases operational costs and reduces consistency. This paper presents a lightweight and fully reproducible dual-agent system for automated product listing generation and multi-turn multilingual customer support. The system integrates two cooperative agents: (1) a Listing Agent capable of generating SEO-friendly multilingual product titles, bullet points, and detailed descriptions; and (2) a Support Agent capable of intent detection, language recognition, FAQ retrieval, and multi-turn conversational responses. Both agents are powered by the DeepSeek large language model (LLM) and deployed via a Gradio-based interface. A small, publicly reproducible demo dataset is constructed to ensure portability and clarity for research and teaching. Experimental demonstrations show that the proposed system produces coherent multilingual listings and maintains context-aware customer dialogues across languages and intents. The proposed approach provides a practical framework for lightweight intelligent e-commerce systems without relying on large proprietary datasets.  © 2025 IEEE.},
