	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105031383887?origin=resultslist},
	doi = {10.1109/SRC65875.2025.11263704},
	abstract = {Often functioning as facilitators or mediators, polyadic chatbots-also known as multiparty conversational agents-simultaneously enable contact with several individuals. While such chatbots are important, most systems concentrate on creating dyadic chatbots for one-on-one interactions. Large language models (LLMs) and their sophisticated natural language processing (NLP) features have allowed expressive dyadic chatbots; nonetheless, the potential of LLMs in polyadic chatbots is still underused. This work presents PolyTalk, a customizable system based on ChatGPT-4 intended to generate polyadic chatbots. PolyTalk increases adaptability and applicability by letting developers set settings such as the opening prompt and conversational length.  © 2025 IEEE.},
